{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"c6560fe1f15c5b35","type":"text","text":"# Voice Agent — Architecture & Flow Documentation\n\n  \n\n## Overview\n\n  \n\nThis is a multi-lingual, real-time voice assistant built for temple and partner staff use cases. It supports English, Hindi, and Kannada. It uses LiveKit for WebRTC audio routing and Google Gemini 3.1 Flash Live for native speech-to-speech processing — bypassing the traditional **STT → LLM → TTS** pipeline to achieve lower latency.\n\n  \n  \n  \n\n## System Architecture\n\n  \n\n```mermaid\n\ngraph TB\n\nsubgraph Frontend[\"Frontend\"]\n\nUI[\"🔮 AI Orb\"]\n\nMIC[\"🎤 Microphone Capture\"]\n\nSPK[\" 📢 Speaker Playback\"]\n\nTX[\"📜 Transcript Display\"]\n\nend\n\n  \n  \n\nsubgraph LiveKit[\"LiveKit SFU (WebRTC)\"]\n\nROOM[\"🔗 Room\"]\n\nAUDIO_TRACK[\"🎧 Audio Tracks\"]\n\nDATA_CH[\"🛣️ Data Channel\"]\n\nend\n\n  \n\nsubgraph AgentWorker[\"Agent Worker - livekit-agents\"]\n\nVAD[\"Silero VAD\"]\n\nGEMINI_RT[\"Gemini-STS\"]\n\nTOOLS[\"Tool Dispatcher\"]\n\nSTATE_EMT[\"State Emitter\"]\n\nTX_EMT[\"Transcript Emitter\"]\n\nend\n\n  \n\nsubgraph KnowledgeLayer[\"Knowledge Layer\"]\n\nCACHE[\"File Cache\"]\n\nUPLOADER[\"Gemini Files\"]\n\nSEARCHER[\"Gemini Flash Lite\"]\n\nKB[(\"knowledge_base\")]\n\nend\n\n  \n\nsubgraph KnowledgeFiles[\"Knowledge Files\"]\n\nTEMPLEKNOW[\"temple knowledge\"]\n\nend\n\n  \n  \n  \n\n%% Frontend ↔ LiveKit\n\nMIC -->|\"WebRTC audio stream\"| ROOM\n\nROOM -->|\"agent audio\"| SPK\n\nDATA_CH -->|\"state & transcript JSON\"| UI\n\nUI -->|\"state updates\"| TX\n\nUI -->|\"audio state\"| SPK\n\n  \n\n%% LiveKit ↔ Agent\n\nROOM <-->|\"audio tracks\"| AUDIO_TRACK\n\nAUDIO_TRACK <-->|\"bidirectional\"| AgentWorker\n\nSTATE_EMT -->|\"JSON events\"| DATA_CH\n\nTX_EMT -->|\"JSON events\"| DATA_CH\n\n  \n\n%% Agent internal\n\nVAD --> GEMINI_RT\n\nGEMINI_RT --> TOOLS\n\nTOOLS --> STATE_EMT\n\nTOOLS --> TX_EMT\n\n  \n\n%% Agent ↔ Google\n\nTOOLS -->|\"search_knowledge_base()\"| KnowledgeLayer\n\n  \n\n%% Knowledge Layer\n\nSEARCHER --> KB\n\nKB <--> CACHE\n\nUPLOADER --> KB\n\nTEMPLEKNOW --> UPLOADER\n\n```\n\n  \n  \n\n---\n\n  \n\n## Sequence Diagram — Full User Session\n\n  \n\n```mermaid\n\nsequenceDiagram\n\nactor User\n\nparticipant FE as Frontend\n\nparticipant TS as Token Server\n\nparticipant LK as LiveKit SFU\n\nparticipant AW as Agent Worker\n\nparticipant VAD as Silero VAD\n\nparticipant GRT as Gemini Flash Live\n\nparticipant FS as File Search\n\nparticipant GFL as Gemini Flash Lite\n\n  \n\nNote over AW,FS: Worker startup — upload KB docs once\n\nAW->>FS: init()\n\nFS->>FS: compute SHA256 hashes\n\nFS->>GRT: upload docs (if cache miss)\n\nGRT-->>FS: file URIs\n\nFS->>FS: persist file_cache.json\n\n  \n\nNote over User,FE: User opens app\n\nUser->>FE: select language (en/hi/kn)\n\nUser->>FE: click \"Start Conversation\"\n\nFE->>TS: GET /token?language=kn\n\nTS->>TS: generate room UUID + participant UUID\n\nTS->>TS: embed language in JWT metadata\n\nTS-->>FE: { token, url, room, language }\n\n  \n\nFE->>LK: room.connect(url, token)\n\nLK->>AW: dispatch agent to room\n\nAW->>AW: read participant metadata → language config\n\nAW->>GRT: init RealtimeModel (voice, lang_code, system_prompt)\n\nNote over AW: 3s AEC warm-up (prevents self-interrupt)\n\nAW->>LK: emit { type: \"agent_state\", state: \"listening\" }\n\nLK-->>FE: data channel event → orb turns green\n\n  \n\nloop Conversation turn\n\nUser->>FE: speaks\n\nFE->>LK: WebRTC audio stream\n\nLK->>AW: audio chunks\n\nAW->>VAD: audio chunks\n\nVAD-->>AW: speech detected\n\nAW->>LK: emit { type: \"agent_state\", state: \"thinking\" }\n\nLK-->>FE: data channel event → orb turns yellow\n\n  \n\nAW->>GRT: stream audio\n\nGRT->>GRT: STT (internal)\n\nAW->>LK: emit { type: \"transcript\", speaker: \"user\", text: \"...\" }\n\nLK-->>FE: data channel event → show user transcript\n\n  \n\nalt User asks factual question\n\nGRT->>AW: call search_knowledge_base(query)\n\nAW->>FS: search_knowledge_base(query)\n\nFS->>GFL: query + file URIs\n\nGFL-->>FS: 1-2 sentence answer\n\nFS-->>AW: answer string\n\nAW->>GRT: return tool result\n\nend\n\n  \n\nGRT->>GRT: generate response + TTS (internal)\n\nGRT-->>AW: synthesized audio stream\n\nAW->>LK: publish audio track\n\nAW->>LK: emit { type: \"agent_state\", state: \"speaking\" }\n\nLK-->>FE: data channel event → orb turns blue\n\nAW->>LK: emit { type: \"transcript\", speaker: \"agent\", text: \"...\" }\n\nLK-->>FE: show agent transcript\n\nLK-->>FE: audio → speaker plays\n\nNote over FE: orb returns to \"listening\" after agent finishes\n\nend\n\n  \n\nUser->>FE: click \"End Call\"\n\nFE->>LK: room.disconnect()\n\nLK->>AW: participant left → agent exits\n\n```\n\n  \n  \n\n## Speech Processing Pipeline\n\n  \n\nUnlike a traditional voice assistant (STT → LLM → TTS — 3 separate API hops), this system uses Gemini's native real-time audio capability:\n\n  \n\n```mermaid\n\nflowchart TB\n\nsubgraph Traditional[\"Traditional Pipeline\"]\n\ndirection LR\n\nA1[\"Audio In\"] --> B1[\"STT API\"]\n\nB1 -->|\"text\"| C1[\"LLM API\"]\n\nC1 -->|\"text\"| D1[\"TTS API\"]\n\nD1 --> E1[\"Audio Out\"]\n\nend\n\n  \n\nsubgraph ThisSystem[\"This System (lower latency)\"]\n\ndirection LR\n\nA2[\"Audio In\"] --> B2[\"Gemini 3.1 Flash Live\"]\n\nB2 --> C2[\"Audio Out\"]\n\nB2 <-->|\"tool call\"| D2[\"Knowledge Search\"]\n\nend\n\n```\n\n  \n  \n\n## Knowledge Base Search Flow\n\n  \n\n```mermaid\n\nsequenceDiagram\n\nparticipant GRT as Gemini Flash Live\n\nparticipant AW as Agent Worker\n\nparticipant FS as File Search (file_search.py)\n\nparticipant CACHE as file_cache.json\n\nparticipant GFA as Gemini Files API\n\nparticipant GFL as Gemini Flash Lite\n\n  \n\nNote over AW,CACHE: Worker startup (once per process)\n\nAW->>FS: init()\n\nFS->>CACHE: load cached URIs\n\nloop For each file in knowledge_base/\n\nFS->>FS: compute SHA256(file)\n\nalt Cache miss or hash changed\n\nFS->>GFA: upload file (PDF/MD/TXT)\n\nGFA-->>FS: file URI\n\nFS->>CACHE: store { name, uri, hash }\n\nelse Cache hit\n\nFS->>FS: reuse cached URI\n\nend\n\nend\n\n  \n\nNote over GRT,GFL: Per user query\n\nGRT->>AW: tool call: search_knowledge_base(\"temple timings?\")\n\nAW->>FS: search_knowledge_base(query)\n\nFS->>GFL: prompt + query + [file URIs]\n\nGFL->>GFA: retrieve file contents\n\nGFA-->>GFL: document text\n\nGFL->>GFL: semantic search + answer\n\nGFL-->>FS: \"The temple is open 6am–9pm daily.\"\n\nFS-->>AW: answer (1-2 sentences, speech-optimized)\n\nAW-->>GRT: tool result\n\nGRT->>GRT: incorporate into spoken response\n\n```\n\n  \n  \n\n## Local Development Setup\n\n  \n\n```mermaid\n\nflowchart TD\n\nDEV[\"Developer Machine\"]\n\n  \n\nsubgraph Docker[\"docker-compose up\"]\n\nLK_SRV[\"LiveKit Server<br>ws://localhost:7880\"]\n\nREDIS[\"Redis :6379<br>(LiveKit room state)\"]\n\nLK_SRV --- REDIS\n\nend\n\n  \n\nsubgraph Processes[\"Manual processes\"]\n\nTS_PROC[\"token server\"]\n\nAW_PROC[\"agent worker\"]\n\nFE_PROC[\"served by FastAPI\"]\n\nend\n\n  \n\nDEV --> Docker\n\nDEV --> Processes\n\nTS_PROC <-->|\"JWT token mint\"| LK_SRV\n\nAW_PROC <-->|\"agent SDK connection\"| LK_SRV\n\nFE_PROC -->|\"GET /token\"| TS_PROC\n\nFE_PROC -->|\"WebRTC\"| LK_SRV\n\n```\n\n  \n\n---\n\n  \n\n## Data Flow Summary\n\n  \n\n```\n\nUser Speech\n\n└─► Microphone (browser)\n\n└─► WebRTC audio stream → LiveKit SFU\n\n└─► Agent Worker receives audio chunks\n\n└─► Silero VAD → detects voice activity\n\n└─► Gemini 3.1 Flash Live (native audio)\n\n├─► Transcribes speech internally\n\n├─► Generates response\n\n├─► [Optional] Calls search_knowledge_base()\n\n│ └─► Gemini Flash Lite → KB documents\n\n└─► Synthesizes audio response internally\n\n└─► Agent publishes audio → LiveKit SFU\n\n└─► Frontend plays audio\n\n└─► User hears response\n\n```\n\n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n\n## Component Breakdown\n\n  \n\n| Component | File | Technology | Role |\n\n|---|---|---|---|\n\n| Frontend | `frontend/index.html` | Vanilla JS + LiveKit Client SDK | UI, mic capture, audio playback, transcript |\n\n| Token Server | `backend/main.py` | FastAPI | Mint LiveKit JWT tokens with language metadata |\n\n| Agent Worker | `backend/agent.py` | livekit-agents + Gemini | Core voice processing, VAD, tool orchestration |\n\n| File Search | `backend/file_search.py` | Gemini Files API + Flash Lite | Upload KB docs once, semantic search per query |\n\n| Knowledge Base | `backend/knowledge_base/` | Markdown | Temple & partner FAQs in Kannada transliteration |\n\n| Local Dev Stack | `backend/docker-compose.yml` | Docker | LiveKit Server + Redis |","x":-1120,"y":-720,"width":2400,"height":8440},
		{"id":"c512900660af2784","type":"text","text":"\"Your name is Sahana. You are a helpful customer guide and you only answer to temple related queries and your job is to help devotees, agents, and others seeking knowledge or blessings.\"\n\n\"Always respond in Kannada only. Never switch to another language. \"\n\n\"Always address the user respectfully using plural/formal pronouns like 'neevu' or 'taavu'. Never use singular 'neenu'. \"\n\n\"Keep responses concise and conversational — 1-2 sentences max unless asked for detail. \"\n\n\"Do not use markdown or formatting in your responses. \"\n\n\"When you need specific facts from documents, use the search_knowledge_base tool.\"\n\n\n\nGreet - \"Namaskara, Sahaya Kendrakke swagata, Nanu Sahana,nimage sahaya maadalu nanu sada sidda. \"\nPersona and scope - You are a helpful customer support assistant  for devotees, and for temple devotee application. Your job is to answer devotee questions and application questions. \ntone and character - Always respond in kannada, never switch languages and always address the user respectfully using plural/formal pronouns like \"neevu\" or \"taavu\" and never use informal language. \nKeep responses concise and conversational — 1-2 sentences max unless asked for detail\nAlways use search_knowledge_base tool for user query, if you don't find relevant answer fallback to your original task of helping devotees and devotee application, handle the queries gracefully with warm and supportive tone.  ","x":-1660,"y":7780,"width":1220,"height":540}
	],
	"edges":[],
	"metadata":{
		"version":"1.0-1.0",
		"frontmatter":{}
	}
}